-- title:
--   Deuring's marked deformation over a formal disc, level three
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a local integral domain of characteristic zero, $k$ an algebraically closed field, and $\pi\colon\mathcal O\to k$ a surjective ring homomorphism with respect to whose kernel $\mathcal O$ is adically complete; assume $3\neq0$ in $k$. Let $W$ be an elliptic Weierstrass curve over $k$, $n\in\mathbb N$ with $2n+1\neq0$ in $k$ and $2n+1$ not a perfect square, $Q_0$ a point of the affine curve of exact additive order $2n+1$, and $\gamma_0$ a Weierstrass variable change over $k$ with $\gamma_0\cdot W$ equal to the Vélu quotient of $W$ by the summing set $\{$coordinates of $kQ_0: 1\le k\le n\}$ (the point at infinity being recorded as $(0,0)$), i.e. the curve with the same $a_1,a_2,a_3$ and with $a_4-5t$, $a_6-b_2t-7w$ for $t,w$ the sums of `veluT`, `veluW` over that set. Let $(x_1,y_1)$, $(x_2,y_2)$ be nonsingular affine points with $3\cdot(x_i,y_i)=0$ and $x_1\neq x_2$. Then there exist an elliptic Weierstrass curve $E$ over $\mathcal O[[T]]$ whose image under $\pi\circ(T\mapsto0)$ is $W$ and whose $j$-invariant reduces to a non-constant power series over $k$; a monic $h\in\mathcal O[[T]][X]$ dividing $E.\mathrm{pre}\Psi'(2n+1)$ and reducing to $\prod_{P}(X-x_P)$ over that summing set, with Kohel quotient $E.\mathrm{kohelQuotient}\,h$ (the Vélu-type quotient formed from $t=6h.\mathrm{rootPowerSumTwo}+b_2h.\mathrm{rootPowerSumOne}+(\deg h)b_4$ and $w=10h.\mathrm{rootPowerSumThree}+2b_2h.\mathrm{rootPowerSumTwo}+3b_4h.\mathrm{rootPowerSumOne}+(\deg h)b_6$) elliptic and reducing to $\gamma_0\cdot W$; and power series $e_1,f_1,e_2,f_2,e'_1,f'_1,e'_2,f'_2$ such that $(e_i,f_i)$ satisfies the affine equation of $E$ and $(e'_i,f'_i)$ that of the Kohel quotient, each $e_i$, $e'_i$ is a root of the corresponding $\Psi_3$, all four values of `deuringA₃` at these points are units, the constant coefficients of $e_i,f_i$ reduce to $x_i,y_i$ and those of $e'_i,f'_i$ to $u_0^{-2}(x_i-r_0)$ and $u_0^{-3}(y_i-t_0-s_0(x_i-r_0))$, and finally the difference of level-three moduli $\delta=(E.\mathrm{kohelQuotient}\,h).\mathrm{levelThreeModulus}\,e'_1f'_1e'_2-E.\mathrm{levelThreeModulus}\,e_1f_1e_2$ (each term of the form $\mathrm{deuringA}_1(x,y)\cdot(x_2-x)\cdot\mathrm{deuringA}_3(x,y)^{-1}$) has constant coefficient in $\ker\pi$ while its coefficientwise reduction along $\pi$ is nonzero.
--
--   This is the deformation-theoretic half of Deuring's lifting theorem, arranged for use in residue characteristic $2$: a non-isotrivial deformation of $W$ over the formal disc is produced together with a lift of the étale cyclic subgroup generated by $Q_0$ (as a monic factor of the division polynomial) and lifts of the two three-torsion points on the curve and on its quotient, the level-three moduli of the two marked curves agreeing exactly at the closed point. It is used by [`WeierstrassCurve.exists_valuationSubring_lift_variableChange_veluQuotient_apply_threeTorsion_eq_of_smul_eq_veluQuotient`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.exists_valuationSubring_lift_variableChange_veluQuotient_apply_threeTorsion_eq_of_smul_eq_veluQuotient).
